2. Who may use the Software for free

The license in section 1 is free of charge for:

  a. individuals;
  b. non-profit organizations, educational institutions and government
     bodies; and
  c. any other organization whose annual gross revenue, together with that
     of all its affiliates, is below the Revenue Threshold.

3. Organizations at or above the Revenue Threshold

An organization whose annual gross revenue, together with that of all its
affiliates, is at or above the Revenue Threshold may evaluate the Software
for up to 30 days. Any other use by such an organization, including
production use and use to provide services to others, requires a separate
commercial license from the licensor. Contact the licensor through
https://github.com/hasirciogluhq/atellar to obtain one.

If an organization reaches the Revenue Threshold while using the Software
under section 2, it has 60 days from the end of the fiscal year in which it
reached the threshold to obtain a commercial license or stop using the
Software.

4. Definitions

"Annual gross revenue" means total revenue from all sources, before any
deductions, in the organization's most recently completed fiscal year,
converted to United States dollars at the exchange rate in effect on the
last day of that fiscal year.

"Affiliate" means any entity that controls, is controlled by, or is under
common control with the organization, where "control" means ownership of
more than 50% of the voting interests or the power to direct management.

